All monsters you want to hit are guaranteed to be within two cursor
moves of you; if you are in a mob and whacking over the top of, say,
insects to get to priests, it's a couple extra keystrokes.

Which admittedly is relatively trivial, but then, it was only a few
keystrokes before too, and people didn't like _that_... so in this case,
rather than try to be too clever at guessing what the user wants, we just say
"OK, we KNOW you don't want the dead monster anymore, so we're reverting
you to default."

